  "label": "Duel of two home-grown talents\n\nThe Nackenheim coach was also happy with the performance of Akhmed Aibuev, who prevailed in the up to 98 kg class (freestyle) with a 16:6 score against the undefeated [Gruppe 1] Akhmed Magamaev this season. \"Wrestled really strongly,\" Ferdinand attested. However, the SVA athletes also came up short in several duels where athletes met on equal footing. For example, in the fight of the home-grown talents (75 kg, freestyle), in which Nackenheim's Koray Cakici desperately wanted to secure his first victory of the season, but allowed himself to be outmaneuvered by his opponent too often and lost 2:10. His brother Kubilay Cakici also remained unsuccessful, losing 2:8 against Burghausen's Ali-Pasha Umarpashaev (80 kg, freestyle) - albeit under curious circumstances. This is because at an intermediate score of 2:4, the referee accidentally blew the whistle, which visibly irritated the athletes. Before Cakici realized what was happening, he was turned by the faster-reacting [Gruppe 1]. The score counted. \"That was not right,\" Robin Ferdinand said angrily."
